  "title": "Kourovka problem 18.44 (main)",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "Let G be a finite non-abelian group and V a finite faithful irreducible G-\nmodule. Suppose that M = |G/G′ | is the largest orbit size of G on V , and among\norbits of G on V there are exactly two orbits of size M . Does this imply that G is\ndihedral of order 8, and |V | = 9?                                     T. M. Keller",
